HIUSA-EXCESS

# Logs and captured shell output - never source of truth, machine-specific
*.log

# Word/Office owner-lock temp files
~$*

# Raw DB dumps - the 44 migrations under server/database/migrations are the
# source of truth for schema; a dump goes stale the moment a migration lands.
*.sql

# User-uploaded financial/media artifacts (GCash QR, payment proof, partylist
# and merchandise images) - runtime data, not source. Keep the directories so
# the app has somewhere to write and serve /uploads/... from on a fresh clone.
server/public/uploads/*
!server/public/uploads/*/
server/public/uploads/*/*
!server/public/uploads/*/.gitkeep
# demo-* assets ARE tracked: the seeders reference them by path, so a fresh
# clone needs them present or the app stores a URL that 404s.
!server/public/uploads/*/demo-*